<title>ITALY: SOCCER-ITALIAN FIRST DIVISION SCORERS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ITALIAN FIRST DIVISION SCORERS.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scorers in Italian first division after matches on Sunday:</p>
<p>18 - Filippo Inzaghi (Atalanta)</p>
<p>14 - Abel Balbo (Roma), Vincenzo Montella (Sampdoria)</p>
<p>13 - Roberto Mancini</p>
<p>12 - Gabriel Batistuta (Fiorentina), Marcelo Otero (Vicenza)</p>
<p>11 - Youri Djorkaeff (Inter)</p>
<p>10 - Giuseppe Signori (Lazio)</p>
<p> 9 - Enrico Chiesa (Parma), Paolo Poggi (Udinese), Sandro</p>
<p>     Tovalieri (Cagliari), George Weah (Milan)</p>
<p> 8 - Alessandro Del Piero and Michele Padovano (both Juventus),</p>
<p>     Igor Kolyvanov (Bologna), Pasquale Luiso (Piacenza), Filippo</p>
<p>     Maniero (Verona)</p>
<p> 7 - Anselmo Robbiati (Fiorentina), Oliver Bierhoff (Udinese),</p>
<p>     Marco Negri (Perugia)</p>
<p> 6 - Alfredo Aglietti (Napoli), Marco Amoroso (Udinese),</p>
<p>     Roberto Murgita (Vicenza), Luis Oliveira (Fiorentina)</p>
<p> 5 - Demetrio Albertini (Milan), Nicola Caccia and Andre Cruz</p>
<p>     (both  Napoli), Marco Carparelli (Sampdoria), Giampiero Maini</p>
<p>     (Vicenza), Roberto Muzzi (Cagliari), Pierluigi Orlandini</p>
<p>     (Verona), Igor Simutenkov (Reggiana)</p>
